<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr CPI flat at 19.5 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr CPI flat at 19.5 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 1.4 percent in October against a 1.9 percent rise in September, keeping year-on-year inflation flat at 19.5 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>CPI rose 15.5 percent in the January-October period, compared with a 18.3 percent rise in the corresponding period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES    OCTOBER   SEPTEMBER   OCT 1995</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)    1.4	 1.9	     1.8</p>
<p> yr/yr change		   19.5	19.5	    22.4</p>
<p> services m/m change	   1.6	 1.3	     0.9</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	19.8	18.9	    22.1</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	1.2	 2.7	     2.5</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change   19.9	20.2	    19.9</p>
<p>NOTES - previously announced data in brackets</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
